Output :error: type argument String is not within bounds of type-variable TMultiple BoundsMultiple Bounds can restrict a type to inherit from one class and implement multiple interfaces.The class must come first.You can’t use more than one class in the bounds.Example: <T extends ClassName & Interface1 & Interface2>Syntax:<T extends superClassName & Interface>Example:  Bound Type Parameters using multiple bounds in Generics (T extends A & B)
            Java

    class Bound<T extends A & B>
{
    private T objRef;

    public Bound(T obj){
        this.objRef = obj;
    }

    public void doRunTest(){
        this.objRef.displayClass();
    }
}
